 # Single-View Depth Shape Completion
 
-Also called: DeepSDF Optimization with Adaptive Sampling
+Also called: DeepSDF Optimization with Adaptive Sampling, Reconstruction from Single-view Depth Maps
 
 ## Overview
-Recovers a complete 3D shape from a single depth image by optimizing a latent code through a differentiable renderer, requiring no additional training of the shape generator [S1, S2]. It sets itself apart from its sibling [DeepSDF](link) by replacing fixed-distance sampling with adaptive sampling via differentiable sphere tracing, which better captures boundaries and thin structures [S1]. It differs from [Differentiable Sphere Tracing](2316-differentiable-sphere-tracing.md) by explicitly combining a Directional Distance Function (DDF) for ray intersection with a Signed Distance Function (SDF) for loss computation, avoiding standard sphere tracing iterations [S2].
+Recovers a complete 3D shape from a single depth image by optimizing a latent code through a differentiable renderer, requiring no additional training of the shape generator [S1, S2]. It sets itself apart from its sibling [DeepSDF](52-deepsdf.md) by replacing fixed-distance sampling with adaptive sampling via differentiable sphere tracing, which better captures boundaries and thin structures [S1]. It differs from [Differentiable Sphere Tracing](2316-differentiable-sphere-tracing.md) by explicitly combining a Directional Distance Function (DDF) for ray intersection with a Signed Distance Function (SDF) for loss computation, avoiding standard sphere tracing iterations [S2].
 
